# Recovered payloads must round-trip byte-for-byte.
#
# The Lua, C#, Java and config-table trees are machine-generated decompiler
# output, not hand-written text. Letting git apply its text/eol heuristics
# (CRLF<->LF normalisation) could rewrite line endings - or mishandle a file
# whose bytes git misjudges - which would silently diverge from the APK the
# tree was decoded from. `-text` disables that class of corruption everywhere.
* -text

# The hand-written toolchain is the opposite case: real text, real diffs, and LF
# endings wanted on every platform. These paths are scoped rather than matched
# by extension on purpose - a global `*.json text` rule would also rewrite the
# 7,390 recovered Unity JSON files under source-app/unity-assets.
*.sh          text eol=lf
/tools/**     text eol=lf
/.github/**   text eol=lf
/*.md         text eol=lf